{"name":"Window Box","hex":"#bcafbb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"window box","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A narrow box filled with earth, placed on a windowsill and used for growing plants.","One of the hollows in the sides of a window frame for the weights which counterbalance a lifting sash."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/window_box"}],"entries":[{"title":"Window box","blocks":[{"text":"A window box is a type of flower container for live flowers or plants in the form of a box attached on or just below the sill of a window. It may also be used for growing herbs or other edible plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/My_favorite_window_box_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-My_favorite_window_box_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_box","wikidata":"Q23583755"},{"title":"Window","blocks":[{"text":"A window is an opening in a wall, door, roof, or vehicle that allows the exchange of light and sometimes allows the passage of sound and air. Modern windows are usually glazed, or covered in some other transparent or translucent material, a sash set in a frame in the opening. The sash and frame are also referred to as a window. Many glazed windows may be opened, to allow ventilation, or closed to exclude inclement weather. Windows may have a latch or similar mechanism to lock the window shut or to hold it open by various amounts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Atua_Kosua_shrine4.jpg/330px-Atua_Kosua_shrine4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window","wikidata":"Q35473"},{"title":"Box","blocks":[{"text":"A box is a container with rigid sides used for the storage or transportation of its contents. Most boxes have flat, parallel, rectangular sides. Boxes can be very small or very large and can be used for a variety of purposes, from functional to decorative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif/lossy-page1-330px-L%C3%A5da_-_Livrustkammaren_-_107142.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Box","wikidata":"Q188075"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/2000_Valparaiso_Chile_4665212086_5519a3ae2b_o.jpg/250px-2000_Valparaiso_Chile_4665212086_5519a3ae2b_o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/2000_Valparaiso_Chile_4665212086_5519a3ae2b_o.jpg/250px-2000_Valparaiso_Chile_4665212086_5519a3ae2b_o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2000_Valparaiso_Chile_4665212086_5519a3ae2b_o.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg/330px-2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg/960px-2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg/330px-2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2006_Tokyo_164160974_30332e8d6e_o.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Black_Horse_Inn_patio_window_box_in_Nuthurst_West_Sussex_England.jpg/330px-Black_Horse_Inn_patio_window_box_in_Nuthurst_West_Sussex_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con